Package: TriGer
Type: Package
Title: Structured Cross-Omics Interaction Discovery with a Triple-Graph Model
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Jiaao", family = "Yu", email = "jy2941@umd.edu",
        role = "aut"),
    person(given = "Huang", family = "Lin",
        email = "huanglinfrederick@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4892-7871")))
Description: Detects modules of features that are densely associated across
    two omics layers and coherent within each layer. Dense cross-omics blocks
    are found by greedy peeling of the cross-omics association matrix, and
    large blocks are refined by greedy peeling of the within-omics
    correlation matrices. Input can be numeric matrices or
    SummarizedExperiment objects. Plotting functions show the detected
    modules alongside the within-omics correlation structure. The method is
    described in Yu, Lin and Chen (2026) <doi:10.64898/2026.09.10.749540>.
